      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments,\" causing ingestion normalization issues and Rules Engine matching failures. Jin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a config-only change, hot-reloadable, low risk, and does not require changes to Okta flows or appliance restarts during settlement windows. This approach avoids waiting for the longer Okta change control process, which could take 2\u20134 weeks. [art_79f625aafa16, art_e60697c15fce]",
